<question type="description"><name><text>Module 2 · Lesson 7 · Section 7: The Story — Part 7</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text><![CDATA[<h3>Section 7: The Story — Part 7</h3>
<p><strong>The Summons</strong></p>
<p><em>Narrative note: Pay attention to the massive use of weak
roots—ʾemar (said), ʾezal (went), īdaʿ (knew), hwā (was/became), ḥzaw
(they saw), ʾetā (came).</em></p>
<p><strong>Sentence 1</strong></p>
<p>ܟܕ ܐܡܪ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܡܠܬܐ ܕܐܠܗܐ، ܐܙܠܘ ܩܫܝܫܐ ܠܘܬ ܡܠܟܐ kad ʾemar Yūḥannan meltā
d-Alāhā, ʾezalū qašīšē l-wāt malkā. kad (when) ʾemar (said) Yūḥannan
(John) meltā (the-word) d-Alāhā (of-God), ʾezalū (went) qašīšē
(the-elders/guards) l-wāt (to-the-presence-of) malkā (the-king). → When
Yukhannan said the word of God, the guards went to the king.</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 2</strong></p>
<p>ܐܡܪܝܢ ܠܗ ܝܕܥܝܢ ܚܢܢ ܡܐ ܗܘܐ ܒܬܪܥܐ ʾāmrīn l-eh: yādʿīn-ḥnan mā hwā
b-tarʿā! ʾāmrīn (they-[are]-saying) l-eh (to-him): yādʿīn (knowing)
-ḥnan (are-we) mā (what) hwā (happened/was) b-tarʿā (in-the-gate)! →
They say to him: “We know what happened at the gate!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 3</strong></p>
<p>ܚܙܝܢ ܓܒܪܐ ܘܐܡܪ ܡܠܬܐ ܒܝܫܬܐ ḥzayn gabrā, w-ʾemar meltā bīštā. ḥzayn
(we-saw) gabrā (a-man), w-ʾemar (and-said) meltā (a-word) bīštā
(evil-[f]). → “We saw a man, and he said an evil word.”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 4</strong></p>
<p>ܗܘܐ ܗܫܐ ܡܠܟܐ ܪܓܝܙ ܛܒ hwā hāšā malkā ragīz ṭāb. hwā (became/was) hāšā
(now) malkā (the-king) ragīz (angry) ṭāb (greatly/very). → Now the king
was very angry.</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 5</strong></p>
<p>ܐܡ̣ܪ ܡܠܟܐ ܠܩܫܝܫܐ ܐܝܬܝܘܗܝ ܠܗܪܟܐ ʾemar malkā l-qašīšē: ʾaytāw-hy
l-harkā! ʾemar (said) malkā (the-king) l-qašīšē (to-the-guards):
ʾaytāw-hy (let-them-bring-him [Aphel imperative]) l-harkā (to-here)! →
The king said to the guards: “Bring him here!”</p>
<p><strong>Sentence 6</strong></p>
<p>ܘܐܬܐ ܝܘܚܢܢ ܩܕܡ ܡܠܟܐ w-ʾetā Yūḥannan qdām malkā. w-ʾetā (and-came)
Yūḥannan (John) qdām (before) malkā (the-king). → And Yukhannan came
before the king.</p>
